Description of the solution applied from the AWS management console.
a--
Register 3 VPCs and 3 instances in Amazon EC2, one for each of the pet store servers.

b--
Activate a VPC and an instance in EFS by making the most appropriate configuration.
Create a security group that ensures that communication will only occur with the 3 servers of the 3 stores.

c--
On one of the instances EC2 in one of the availability zones, make a peer-to-peer connection to the EFS instance.

d--
Then make the connection from EFS to the EC2 instance

e--
Perform the same process with each of the servers in the other availability zones

note:
The connection will always be between each of the store server instances and the EFS instance in the cloud, never directly between the servers.

business opportunity:
With files centralized in a cloud instance, the opportunity opens up to offer online services for selling products to pet owners. Similarly, 
web-based services such as scheduling appointments and issuing promotions, for example, can be offered.
